.TH LSA 1 "October 2026" "lsa-sysinfo 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lsa \- Linux System Audit cache and memory benchmark (command line)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lsa cachemem
[\fB\-\-threads\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-seconds\fR \fIS\fR] [\fB\-\-isa\fR avx512|avx2|sse2] [\fB\-\-mem\-mib\fR \fIM\fR]
[\fB\-\-only\fR mem|l1|l2|l3[,..]] [\fB\-\-tests\fR read,write,copy,latency] [\fB\-\-mib\fR]
[\fB\-\-mem\-write\fR auto|clzero|stream] [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
.br
.B lsa guide
[\fIITEM\fR] [\fB\-\-print\fR]
.br
.B lsa guide \-\-list
.br
.B lsa \-\-version
|
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Linux System Audit is a clean-room Linux implementation of AIDA64 Business
features (AIDA64 is by FinalWire Ltd.; not affiliated).
.B lsa cachemem
measures read, write and copy bandwidth (MB/s) and latency (ns) of memory and
the L1, L2 and L3 caches. It uses every CPU thread and the memory bus for about
20 seconds, so it asks before it starts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-yes ", " \-y
Start without asking (for scripts). Without a terminal and without
.B \-\-yes
the benchmark does not start and
.B lsa
exits with code 2.
.TP
.B \-\-mib
Show the results in MiB/s and GiB/s (1024-based) instead of MB/s and GB/s.
.TP
.BR \-\-isa ", " \-\-only ", " \-\-tests ", " \-\-mem\-write
Choose the code path, the levels, the tests and the memory write method. An
unknown value stops with a message listing the valid ones (exit code 2).
.PP
Run
.B lsa \-\-help
for the meaning of each option.
.SH GUIDE
.B lsa guide
\fIITEM\fR opens the user guide at the section for one result or system line,
for example
.B lsa guide mem-latency
or
.BR "lsa guide cpu-fsb" .
.B \-\-list
lists the items,
.B \-\-print
shows the command that would be run instead of running it. The guide is
installed as /usr/share/doc/lsa-sysinfo/LSA-User-Guide.pdf and
/usr/share/doc/lsa-sysinfo/html/LSA-User-Guide.html.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the test memory cannot be allocated or the guide cannot
be opened, 2 for a usage error or when the benchmark was not started.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lsa-gui (1)
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://github.com/eugenesflanagin-spec/lsa-sysinfo
